    handoff = '# X50 handoff\n\n' + lead + '\n\nFour designs run. R2 : s deep bite test-ROC sensitivity 0,845 at Sp0,90 and 0,825 at Sp0,95 ; frozen calibration only reaches Sp0,831 / 0,910 . R4 : s all-region opening 21 / 173 positive/ negative , 18 / 21 ( Sp0,931 ) and 17 / 21 ( Sp0,948 ), all screening gates FAIL . Angle III19 and saxbett 9 positive -> minimum requirements UNKNOWN . All inter/intra-noise floor UNKNOWN .\n\n' + '\n'.join(table) + _release_expand('\n\nPrecise raw values : results.json and raw/RESULTS_R1..R4.json ; patient/source locators in raw labels and EXTERNAL_LOCATORS . `./run_all.sh` run reproducible comparison, controls , demo and figures. Thresholds /models/ PREREG is frozen and may not be replaced. Distributions are descriptive according to previous test exposure.\n\nWhat failed : low FN tolerance at high specificity, transfer of specificity thresholds, minimum for rare findings, identification of rat noise. @DENTAL_CASE_ID@ showed that anteriora reference is insufficient for any region issue; R4 preserves the improvement in observation range and new misses. The adequacy tests have identity error 0 and downstream differences 1,0,2 and 1.\n\nThe next design to run is region/per tooth blind new measurement according to MEASUREMENT_SPEC.md . Use FROZEN_MEASUREMENT_PANEL.json for source freeze; new patients are needed for external validation. Register assess-ID /time and at least two repeated poses; do not re-adjust to old test data. Four-round artifacts may be working documents, not scientific admission.\n\nGrafcoverage is missing for finding specific betscreening. Proposed nod DENT - VAL - BITE - FINDING - SCREENING ( PROPOSAL_ONLY ), consumer DENT - GOAL , PER_TOOTH / Region Report -> PER_ARCH aggregation, SIMULTANEOUS . DENT - VAL - OCCLUSAL - REGIONAL - FORCES is force and must not wear a screening clause. GRAPH_FEEDBACK.json with null target and PENDING_INDEPENDENT_REVIEW , no native graph dispatch/feedback to wrong target node.\n')
    (P / 'HANDOFF.md').write_text(handoff)
    feedback = dict(lane='X50-bite-screening', target_id=None, review_state='PENDING_INDEPENDENT_REVIEW', result_path=str(P / 'results.json'), result_sha256=sha(P / 'results.json'), measured_quantity='Per-finding sensitivity at empirical Sp .90/.95 and cal-frozen achieved Sp, plus within-case conditional report agreement', units='fraction of PER_ARCH cases, POPULATION confidence intervals', uncertainty='Wilson95 and stratified patient-bootstrap95; report/rater identity and physical pose uncertainty UNKNOWN', population='Inherited X7 case-disjoint train593/cal198/test198; prior test exposure; finding-specific exclusions', frozen_gate='PREREG_R1/R2/R3/R4.json', baseline='Actually refit equal-information HGB and logistic; human report2 conditional consistency; no unaided-clinician praxis measurement', outcome='All screening gates FAIL or UNKNOWN; region-scope extension executed; true noise-floor attainment UNKNOWN', negative_result=True, coverage_state='MISSING_EXACT_SCREENING_TARGET', coverage_proposal='DENT-VAL-BITE-FINDING-SCREENING', resolution='PER_TOOTH/source region -> consumer PER_ARCH; POPULATION rates', timescale='SIMULTANEOUS')
    write(P / 'GRAPH_FEEDBACK.json', feedback)
    write(P / 'GRAPH_COVERAGE_PROPOSAL.json', dict(proposed_id='DENT-VAL-BITE-FINDING-SCREENING', status='PROPOSAL_ONLY', existing_goal='DENT-GOAL', source_artifacts=[_release_expand('X7'), _release_expand('X21'), _release_expand('X50')], missing_quantities=['source-polarity by tooth/region', 'sensitivity at fixed specificity by finding', 'conditional named-reader positive/negative agreement', 'pose-repeat error budget'], edges=[dict(from_quantity='registered tooth-region geometry and clinician region statement', to_quantity='finding-specific screening and referral research evaluation', resolution='PER_TOOTH/PER_SURFACE_REGION', timescale='SIMULTANEOUS')]))
    state('FOUR_CONSTRUCTIONS_DELIVERED', 'All original scientific gates FAIL/UNKNOWN retained; source-scope capability delivered', 'Independent review, then blind regional measurement/new patient validation per MEASUREMENT_SPEC.md')
